# RSI Kernel Agent — Repository Guidance

- Multiple strategies A/B/... may be explored in the same round.
- Each strategy may produce multiple evidence-backed Plans and Candidates.
- Do not force a single winner before experiments.
- Preserve failed, regressed, deferred and successful runs.
- Analyzer is a Profiler child branch.
- Benchmark owns correctness, comparable timing, coverage and promotion.
- Unknown causal explanation does not automatically invalidate a correct, reliably faster candidate.
- Respect approved write scopes and existing user changes.
- Do not alter correctness oracles, tolerances, workloads or timing boundaries to make candidates pass.
- Distinguish measured facts, trace-derived values, compiler estimates, model predictions and hypotheses.
- Never claim TPU validation when only CPU/mock tests ran.
- Keep credentials and local auth stores out of the repository.
